+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
+<Defs>
+  <!-- ============================================================= -->
+  <!-- 量子位元破譯：封存檔案 II 級 · 石碑解碼器                        -->
+  <!-- 解鎖解碼器（DMS_OccultechExtractor）。完成時由                   -->
+  <!-- DMS.ModExtension_ResearchQuest 派發石碑任務線（DMS_Stele），     -->
+  <!-- 研究完成前石碑任務線不會出現。石碑本體放在 FFF_DevCategory，     -->
+  <!-- 玩家只能從任務線取得。                                           -->
+  <!-- ============================================================= -->
+  <ResearchProjectDef>
+    <defName>DMS_Occultech_QubitDecryption</defName>
+    <label>qubit decryption</label>
+    <description>A decoding technique that bypasses a stele's own verification layer and reads its data by directly measuring the quantum state held at each lattice site of its holographic storage plates. The stele's encryption rests on the assumption that no one outside the fleets can observe those quantum states without collapsing them; this technique simply chooses to accept the collapse. Every reading permanently destroys the region it reads. What is recovered can be archived for research, and what is lost can never be restored.\nThe technique was leaked by fleet deviants. Steles are the backup memory of every colonial world, and every stele scanned this way is a record that no one will ever be able to read again.\n\nApproved by ████ and ███, qubit decryption and its related technologies are designated class II sealed technology. Disclosure of such technology is prohibited, and any decoding equipment discovered is to be destroyed on site.</description>
+    <tab>DMS_ExpeditionalKnowledge</tab>
+    <knowledgeCategory>DMS_Sealed</knowledgeCategory>
+    <knowledgeCost>1000</knowledgeCost>
+    <techLevel>Spacer</techLevel>
+    <researchViewX>3.00</researchViewX>
+    <researchViewY>2.00</researchViewY>
+    <prerequisites>
+      <li>MicroelectronicsBasics</li>
+    </prerequisites>
+    <discoveredLetterTitle>Sealed file II: qubit decryption</discoveredLetterTitle>
+    <discoveredLetterText>Using the data they have gathered, researchers have finished decoding the sealed technology. It contains a stele decryption technique leaked by fleet deviants.\n\nThe decoder can now be built. Set flush against a stele and supplied with power, it can extract the occultech knowledge stored in the stele.\n\nWith this method in hand, the colony can also trace the occultech glyphs scattered across this world. Recovering the glyphs will lead to a stele.\n\nThe fleets sealed this file to keep the data in the steles out of anyone else's hands. Every stele read this way is a permanent loss to the fleets.</discoveredLetterText>
+    <descriptionHyperlinks>
+      <ThingDef>DMS_OccultechExtractor</ThingDef>
+      <ThingDef>DMS_OccultTechFont</ThingDef>
+    </descriptionHyperlinks>
+    <modExtensions>
+      <li Class="DMS.ModExtension_ResearchQuest">
+        <quest>DMS_Stele</quest>
+      </li>
+    </modExtensions>
+  </ResearchProjectDef>
+
+  <!-- ============================================================= -->
+  <!-- 重型仿生服：封存檔案 I 級 · 密閉突擊外骨骼                       -->
+  <!-- ============================================================= -->
+  <ResearchProjectDef>
+    <defName>DMS_Occultech_BionicSuitHeavy</defName>
+    <label>enclosed assault frame</label>
+    <description>A load-bearing frame anchored directly into the pilot's skeleton, driven by artificial muscle bundles that only draw at full closure. It allows a single soldier to carry and operate armament far beyond their own muscular limit. Because closure is a precondition of output, the device cannot be released by any conventional means once sealed, and separation of the pilot must be performed surgically.\nThis inability to self-release classifies the device, under the laws of war, as restraining equipment upon its own pilot. The positive applications of its skeletal anchoring and load-transfer principles to prosthetic rehabilitation are nonetheless equally present.\n\nApproved by ███████ and ███, the enclosed assault frame and its related technologies are designated class I sealed technology. Sale of such technology to developing worlds is prohibited, and its related technologies are to be progressively declassified once a colonial world's society attains class I standard.</description>
+    <tab>DMS_ExpeditionalKnowledge</tab>
+    <knowledgeCategory>DMS_Restricted</knowledgeCategory>
+    <knowledgeCost>750</knowledgeCost>
+    <techLevel>Spacer</techLevel>
+    <researchViewX>1.00</researchViewX>
+    <researchViewY>3.00</researchViewY>
+    <prerequisites>
+      <li>DMS_Artifuscle</li>
+    </prerequisites>
+    <discoveredLetterTitle>Sealed file I: enclosed assault frame</discoveredLetterTitle>
+    <discoveredLetterText>Using the data they have gathered, researchers have finished decoding the sealed technology.\n\nThe heavy bionic suit can now be assembled at an artifuscle chamber. It lets its pilot carry and operate heavy weapons no ordinary soldier could handle.\n\nIt only works fully closed. Once a pilot is sealed in, it cannot be taken off by normal means and can only be stripped away destructively through surgery.\n\nThe fleets shelved this technology for a reason.</discoveredLetterText>
+    <descriptionHyperlinks>
+      <ThingDef>DMS_Apparel_BionicSuitHeavy</ThingDef>
+      <RecipeDef>DMS_RemoveBionicSuitHeavy</RecipeDef>
+    </descriptionHyperlinks>
+  </ResearchProjectDef>
+
+  <!-- ============================================================= -->
+  <!-- 集群司令：封存檔案 I 級 · 設施級機兵指揮主機              -->
+  <!-- ============================================================= -->
+  <ResearchProjectDef>
+    <defName>DMS_Occultech_GestaltEngine</defName>
+    <label>cluster command</label>
+    <description>A facility-scale computer assembled from arrays of microelectronic chips and the power system that drives them. Even a bare mainframe with no attached subsystems commands and coordinates mechs as capably as a human mechanitor. Technology of this kind was already in wide use in humanity's wars against itself long before it reached the stars, and after the expansion it was deployed in bulk on interstellar terraforming programs, bringing countless barren worlds to life.\n\nApproved by ████ and ██, cluster command and its related technologies are designated class I sealed technology. Provision of such technology to developing worlds is prohibited, and outside emergency war mobilization, standing ground-force deployments are to avoid employing it in any military operation.</description>
+    <tab>DMS_ExpeditionalKnowledge</tab>
+    <knowledgeCategory>DMS_Restricted</knowledgeCategory>
+    <knowledgeCost>750</knowledgeCost>
+    <techLevel>Spacer</techLevel>
+    <researchViewX>1.00</researchViewX>
+    <researchViewY>4.00</researchViewY>
+    <prerequisites>
+      <li>DMS_Mechlink</li>
+    </prerequisites>
+    <discoveredLetterTitle>Sealed file I: cluster command</discoveredLetterTitle>
+    <discoveredLetterText>Using the data they have gathered, researchers have finished decoding the sealed technology: the technical architecture of a cluster command mainframe.\n\nThe central command core can now be built. A single mainframe commands automatroids without a mechanitor, supplying its own control bandwidth and command groups.\n\nBecause the convention caps the personnel that may be committed to a colonial program, the fleets keep this file sealed from standing armies and open it only for emergency mobilization.</discoveredLetterText>
+    <descriptionHyperlinks>
+      <ThingDef>DMS_GestaltEngine</ThingDef>
+    </descriptionHyperlinks>
+  </ResearchProjectDef>
+
+  <!-- ============================================================= -->
+  <!-- 合成生物學：封存檔案 I 級 · 工程菌株有機合成                     -->
+  <!-- ============================================================= -->
+  <ResearchProjectDef>
+    <defName>DMS_Occultech_Biosynthesis</defName>
+    <label>synthetic biology</label>
+    <description>Cultured strains built from the ground up, engineered to reassemble simple nutrients and mineral feedstock into complex organic macromolecules. They synthesize neutroamine, edible artiprotein and comparable organic polymers at far higher efficiency than any conventional process, and require neither fields nor livestock to do it.\n\nApproved by █████ and ███, synthetic biology and its related technologies are designated class I sealed technology. Provision of such technology to developing worlds is prohibited, and derived biosynthesis lines are to be operated only within orbital installations and fleet supply nodes.</description>
+    <tab>DMS_ExpeditionalKnowledge</tab>
+    <knowledgeCategory>DMS_Restricted</knowledgeCategory>
+    <knowledgeCost>750</knowledgeCost>
+    <techLevel>Spacer</techLevel>
+    <researchViewX>1.00</researchViewX>
+    <researchViewY>5.00</researchViewY>
+    <prerequisites>
+      <li>DMS_Artifuscle</li>
+    </prerequisites>
+    <discoveredLetterTitle>Sealed file I: synthetic biology</discoveredLetterTitle>
+    <discoveredLetterText>Using the data they have gathered, researchers have finished decoding the sealed technology. It contains the gene maps and metabolic pathways of a set of engineered culture strains.\n\nArtiprotein can now be refined from crops in a reaction chamber, and neutroamine synthesized from meat and chemfuel. The artifuscle chamber can also grow artificial muscle from artiprotein and tungsteel, with no gold or neutroamine required.\n\nThe fleets did not seal this file over weapons. The large-scale spread of synthesis technology would very likely leave the industries it touches with severe structural unemployment for a long time to come.</discoveredLetterText>
+    <descriptionHyperlinks>
+      <ThingDef>DMS_Artiprotein</ThingDef>
+      <ThingDef>Artifuscle</ThingDef>
+      <ThingDef>Neutroamine</ThingDef>
+    </descriptionHyperlinks>
+  </ResearchProjectDef>
+
+  <!-- ============================================================= -->
+  <!-- 次聲波基礎：封存檔案 I 級 · 次聲波與震波技術                     -->
+  <!-- 前置為原版微電子基礎（MicroelectronicsBasics）。                  -->
+  <!-- ============================================================= -->
+  <ResearchProjectDef>
+    <defName>DMS_Occultech_Subsonic</defName>
+    <label>infrasonics</label>
+    <description>A tuned infrasound device is enough to inflict severe, irreversible damage on the sensory systems of the living things around it, along with pain intense enough to cause shock. The development of infrasonic weapons has therefore been prohibited under the laws of war. The positive applications of infrasonic technology to medicine and geological survey are nonetheless equally present.\n\nApproved by ████ and ██, infrasonics and its related technologies are designated class I sealed technology. Sale of such technology to developing worlds is prohibited, and its related technologies are to be progressively declassified once a colonial world's society attains class I standard.</description>
+    <tab>DMS_ExpeditionalKnowledge</tab>
+    <knowledgeCategory>DMS_Restricted</knowledgeCategory>
+    <knowledgeCost>750</knowledgeCost>
+    <techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
+    <researchViewX>1.00</researchViewX>
+    <researchViewY>6.00</researchViewY>
+    <prerequisites>
+      <li>MicroelectronicsBasics</li>
+    </prerequisites>
+    <discoveredLetterTitle>Sealed file I: infrasonics</discoveredLetterTitle>
+    <discoveredLetterText>Using the data they have gathered, researchers have finished decoding the sealed technology: the design principles of tuned infrasound emitters and seismic survey charges.\n\nFour devices can now be produced: an infrasonic module that gives a mech an area panic ability, an infrasonic emitter tower that periodically drives off nearby enemies, infrasonic grenades that reach every living thing in their radius regardless of walls, and a blast scanner that maps deep ore with a mortar-driven shockwave.\n\nThe blast scanner's shockwave carries far into the ground. Whatever sleeps down there will hear it too.\n\nThe fleets sealed this file because of what these devices do to people. Fielding them openly will be noted.</discoveredLetterText>
+    <descriptionHyperlinks>
+      <ThingDef>DMS_SubsonicModule</ThingDef>
+      <ThingDef>DMS_Building_SubsonicEmitter</ThingDef>
+      <ThingDef>DMS_Weapon_GrenadeSubsonic</ThingDef>
+      <ThingDef>DMS_Building_BlastScanner</ThingDef>
+    </descriptionHyperlinks>
+  </ResearchProjectDef>
+
+  <!-- ============================================================= -->
+  <!-- 駐屯兵器：封存檔案 I 級 · 鬥牛犬與伯勞鳥的生產型號、FPV 無人機母巢 -->
