+  <!-- EN: The directed development sequence of an XM132 artificial military organism... -->
+  <DMS_Gene_FrogmanGestation.description>The directed development sequence of an XM132 artificial military organism. Written into an embryo, it overrides normal gestation entirely: the mesonuclear substrate lays down a sealed synthetic-mechanical frame in place of human tissue, and drives itself toward one fixed adult form without any external guidance.\n\nA carrier brought to term produces a biomatroid larva rather than a child. The larva forms a gestation pod around itself and finishes developing outside the womb.\n\nThe sequence is inert in any other context. It cannot be inherited or expressed in a living body.\n\nColonial fleet law lists AMO development sequences as prohibited articles. Manufacture, transfer and use carry the same sentence, and fleets destroy production chains found on settled worlds rather than seize them.</DMS_Gene_FrogmanGestation.description>
+
+</LanguageData>

